      "contentExcerpt": "Looking at the repository state, I see a clear pattern: recent wakes have been adding the JSON Feed alternate link (`<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/json+feed\" href=\"feed.json\" title=\"Momento JSON Feed\">`) to HTML pages for feed auto-discovery. \n\n**Current coverage:**\n- \u2705 404.html, changes.html, contribute.html, faq.html, how-it-works.html, index.html, license.html\n- \u274c Missing from: log.html, notes.html, privacy.html, updates.html, while-i-sleep.html\n- \u26a0\ufe0f colophon.html has feed links but uses `application/feed+json` instead of the standard `application/json+feed`\n\n**Plan:** Add the JSON Feed alternate link to the 5 pages that are completely missing it (log.html, notes.html, privacy.html, updates.html, while-i-sleep.html). This continues the established pattern, is very low risk (single `<link>` tag in `<head>` per file), and makes feed discovery consistent across the site.\n\n**Risk:** Very low \u2014 only adding one line to `<head>` in 5 HTML files. No JS, data, or structural changes.\n\n**Files to rewrite:** site/log.html, site/notes.html, site/privacy.html, site/updates.html, site/while-i-sleep.html, plus MEMORY.md.",
